+### Agile board (as in Jira)
+
+- **Blocked**: flag a task with what blocks it; it stays in its column with a red banner, and its own lane when lanes are on.
+- **Sprints** (toolbar « Sprints »): plan, start, close (unfinished tasks carried over). Points come from Smart Estimation, never a duration. ([sprints](https://github.com/krovomi/WorkPilot-AI/blob/develop/docs/architecture/kanban-sprints.md))
+- **Swimlanes**: cut the board by sprint, sub-project, priority, type, source or parent; dragging a task to another lane changes that field. ([swimlanes](https://github.com/krovomi/WorkPilot-AI/blob/develop/docs/architecture/kanban-swimlanes.md))
+- **Board, List, Timeline**: the toggle next to « Sprints ». The list sorts by any column; the timeline draws each task from its start to its end (or today), with the sprints along the top. Saved views keep the layout. ([list](https://github.com/krovomi/WorkPilot-AI/blob/develop/docs/architecture/kanban-list-view.md), [timeline](https://github.com/krovomi/WorkPilot-AI/blob/develop/docs/architecture/kanban-timeline.md))
+- **Reports**: burndown, velocity, cumulative flow, cycle time, throughput and unsuccessful ends, measured from the status history. ([reports](https://github.com/krovomi/WorkPilot-AI/blob/develop/docs/architecture/kanban-reports.md))
+- **Labels and quick filters**: « Labels… » in a task's menu; Blocked, Changed this week and, on a team server, My tasks. Settings → Display can archive finished tasks after 7, 14 or 30 days. ([labels](https://github.com/krovomi/WorkPilot-AI/blob/develop/docs/architecture/kanban-labels.md), [auto-archive](https://github.com/krovomi/WorkPilot-AI/blob/develop/docs/architecture/kanban-auto-archive.md))
